A computer sits upon my desk,
Its screen aglow, like a digital nest.
It hums and whirs, a gentle sound,
As it processes information all around.
With keys that click and a mouse that glides,
I navigate worlds, where data resides.
In cyberspace, I find my way,
Through circuits and wires, night and day.
The computer's brain, a complex maze,
Stores secrets, and solves puzzles in daze.
It's a tool, a friend, a guiding light,
That shines so bright, in the dark of night.
So here I'll stay, and work, and play,
With my computer, every single day.

